            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="COL02" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <forename>Henry</forename>
                        <surname>Colburn</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth notBefore="1784" notAfter="1785">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1855-08-16"/>
                    <occupation>publisher</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Colburn began his publishing career at the English and Foreign Circulating Library, London in
      1806. He concentrated on fiction and also published much material in French. In 1814 he
      founded the <title>New Monthly Magazine and Universal Register</title> with Frederic Shoberl
      which became the <title>New Monthly Magazine and Literary Journal</title> in 1821 under the
      stewardship of <persName key="CAM01">Thomas Campbell</persName>.  In 1829 he began a
      partnership with <persName key="BEN01">Richard Bentley</persName> and the <title>Colburn and
      Bentley's Standard Novels</title> series was started - a series which offered cheap reprints of
      contemporary fiction. Under this imprint, Godwin's <title>Caleb Williams</title>, <title>St Leon</title>, and <title>Fleetwood</title> were reissued.</p>
                    </note>
